6.3 Theorem Families Targeted

The following theorem families are targeted for the single-tank pressure control problem:

· T1 (Stability): \dot{V}(x, u^*) \le -\alpha V(x) for some \alpha > 0, where u^* is a specified feedback law.
· T2 (Boundedness): \|x(t)\| \le B for all t \ge 0 under bounded disturbances \|d(t)\| \le d_{\max}.
· T3 (Safety invariance via CBF): If h(x(0)) \ge 0, then h(x(t)) \ge 0 for all t \ge 0.
· T4 (Reduced-order validity): Establish a bounded approximation error \|x_{\text{HF}} - \Pi(z)\| \le \epsilon_{\text{ROM}} over a specified operating region (Theorem 5.1).
· T5 (Observability/identifiability): Given the sensor set (pressure P, temperatures T_L, T_V), the reduced state z is observable. This is a prerequisite for the estimation layer.
· T6 (Hybrid invariance): The hybrid automaton with discrete modes (Idle, Active Cooling, Venting, Pressurizing) maintains forward invariance of the safe set \mathcal{S} = \{x : P_{\min} \le P \le P_{\max}\} across all mode transitions.

6.4 Proof Sketch for T1 (Stability)

Theorem 6.1 (Asymptotic Stability of Pressure Control). Consider the IPHS model with the feedback law Q_{\text{cool}} = -k_P (P - P_{\text{ref}}) and \dot{N}_{\text{press}} = 0. Under the condition that the environmental heat leak Q_{\text{env}} is bounded and k_P > 0 is sufficiently large, the equilibrium pressure P = P_{\text{ref}} is asymptotically stable in the sense of Lyapunov, with Lyapunov function:

V(x) = H(x) + \frac{k_P}{2} (P - P_{\text{ref}})^2.

Proof Sketch. From Theorem 4.1, we have:

\dot{H}(x) \le -T_0 \sigma_s(x) + u^T y + d^T y_d.

With u = Q_{\text{cool}} = -k_P (P - P_{\text{ref}}), the control term becomes:

u^T y = -k_P (P - P_{\text{ref}}) \cdot \left( -\frac{T_L - T_0}{T_L} \right).

Under the quasi-static assumption T_L \approx T_0 (small temperature difference), this term is approximately -k_P (P - P_{\text{ref}}) \cdot 0 = 0, which is insufficient for stability. Therefore, the LLM proposes a modified Lyapunov function that includes a pressure-dependent term:

V(x) = H(x) + \frac{1}{2} \lambda_P (P - P_{\text{ref}})^2,

where \lambda_P > 0. The time derivative is:

\dot{V} = \dot{H} + \lambda_P (P - P_{\text{ref}}) \dot{P}.

Using the pressure dynamics from the IPHS formulation:

\dot{P} = \frac{\partial P}{\partial S_V} \dot{S}_V + \frac{\partial P}{\partial V_V} \dot{V}_V + \frac{\partial P}{\partial N_V} \dot{N}_V,

and substituting the control law, the LLM-guided analysis finds that \dot{V} \le -\alpha V for appropriate choice of \lambda_P and k_P. The formal verification is completed using SOS/SMT tools. \square

