7. Hybrid System Formalization and Verification

Cryogenic pressure control is inherently hybrid: valves open/close, cryocoolers switch modes, and settling thrusters fire intermittently. A purely continuous formulation for V(x) or h(x) fails across discrete mode transitions.

7.1 Hybrid Automaton Model

The cryogenic tank is modeled as a hybrid automaton \mathcal{HA} = (\mathcal{Q}, \mathcal{X}, \mathcal{U}, f, \mathcal{D}, \text{Init}, \text{Guard}), where:

· \mathcal{Q} = \{\text{Idle}, \text{Active Cooling}, \text{Venting}, \text{Pressurizing}\} is the set of discrete modes.
· \mathcal{X} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{11} is the continuous state space.
· \mathcal{U} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^3 is the control input space.
· f_\sigma(x, u) = [J(x) - R(x, e)] e(x) + g(x)u for \sigma \in \mathcal{Q} is the continuous dynamics in each mode.
· \text{Guard} \subseteq \mathcal{Q} \times \mathcal{X} \times \mathcal{Q} defines discrete transition conditions.

```
        P >= P_max (Vent Open)
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                     │
│  ┌───┴──────────┐    ┌───▼──────────┐
│  │ Mode 1: Idle │    │ Mode 2: Vent │
│  └───▲──────────┘    └───┬──────────┘
│       │                   │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
        P <= P_target (Vent Close)
```

7.2 Differential Dynamic Logic (dL) and KeYmaera X

The LLM generates candidate hybrid inductive invariants \phi(x, \sigma), and KeYmaera X verifies forward invariance across both continuous differential equations (\dot{x} = f_\sigma(x, u)) and discrete guard transitions.

Theorem 7.1 (Hybrid Safety Invariance). The hybrid automaton \mathcal{HA} maintains the safe set \mathcal{S} = \{x : P_{\min} \le P \le P_{\max}\} for all time, provided that the CBF condition h(x) \ge 0 is satisfied in each mode and across all guard transitions.

Proof Strategy. The proof uses the dL formula:

[\mathcal{HA}] \, (P_{\min} \le P \le P_{\max}),

where [\mathcal{HA}] is the modal operator for the hybrid automaton. The proof proceeds by induction over the discrete modes, using the continuous CBF condition and the guard conditions to establish invariance across transitions. \square

