Appendix E: Anti-Fabrication and Provenance Logging Schema

E.1 Execution Log Entry

Every tool invocation (e.g., dReal run, SymPy simplification, numerical simulation) is logged with:

```json
{
  "log_id": "uuid",
  "timestamp": "ISO-8601",
  "agent": "Agent_E",
  "tool": "dReal",
  "input": {
    "smt2_file": "sha256:abc123...",
    "parameters": {"delta": 0.001, "timeout": 60}
  },
  "output": {
    "result": "sat",
    "model": {...},
    "stderr": "",
    "return_code": 0
  },
  "reproducible": true,
  "commit_hash": "git:ef567..."
}
```

The SMT2 file is stored in a versioned repository (e.g., Git) with a SHA-256 hash. All intermediate results are stored similarly.

E.2 Mandatory Negative-Result Logging

Each agent must log failed attempts, including:

· Candidate functions that were falsified.
· Proof attempts that failed.
· Literature searches that returned no results.

These are stored in a separate "negative_results" table to ensure transparency and to prevent the system from repeating the same mistakes.

E.3 Anti-Fabrication Metrics Calculation

· Fabrication rate = (number of agent-reported results that fail independent re-execution) / (total number of agent-reported results).
· Negative-result rate = (number of falsified/rejected hypotheses) / (total hypotheses proposed).
· Reproducibility score = (number of final results with complete execution logs and reproducible outputs) / (total number of final results).

These metrics are computed automatically by a separate audit module that re-runs random samples of logged tool calls.

